From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Il tuo nome <tu@esempio.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:11:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: A global reset for the GbE switch, to
 re-enable it

The Ethernet switch reset with a plain host reset (CF9 0x0E), which
disables the GbE but does not bring it back: on a ThinkPad W541, turning
the option off then on cleared BUC bit 5 but the controller stayed
absent ("PCI: Static device PCI: 00:00:19.0 not found"), because the
LAN disable lives in a well that the host reset keeps.

Do a global reset instead (set CF9GR, PMIR/ETR3 bit 20, before CF9
0x0E), as the Lenovo firmware of the W541 does for this option: it
re-initialises the GbE. CF9GR is clear and unlocked in romstage
(early_pch_init_native() clears it later, lpc.c locks it with CF9LOCK in
ramstage), so setting it here takes; if it is locked for any reason, the
host reset still applies a disable, with a warning. The reset happens at
most once per toggle (BUC already holds the wanted value afterward, so
the early return skips it), so there is no loop.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init; on the machine
pending (does the global reset re-enable the GbE with the ME disabled).

Change-Id: Ic4a4e18f6cc2e3069d96e4b4e02cad8948b97643
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_pch.c | 36 +++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_pch.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_pch.c
index 1a3a045bc0..fabd580c11 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_pch.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_pch.c
@@ -104,6 +104,28 @@ void __weak mainboard_config_rcba(void)
  * read-only part, and never on an S3 resume, where a reset would end it.
  */
 #if ENV_SEPARATE_ROMSTAGE
+/*
+ * The reset that applies a change of the LAN disable bit. A plain host reset
+ * (CF9 0x0E) disables the GbE but does not bring it back: the bit is in a well
+ * that the host reset keeps. A global reset (CF9GR set first, then CF9 0x0E)
+ * re-initialises it, as the Lenovo firmware of the W541 does for this option.
+ * CF9GR is clear and unlocked in romstage (early_pch_init_native() clears it
+ * later, lpc.c locks it in ramstage), so set it here. If it is locked for any
+ * reason, fall back to the host reset, which at least applies a disable.
+ */
+static void gbe_reset(void)
+{
+	if (CONFIG(CMOS_POST)) {
+		cmos_post_extra(0x47624500);	/* "GbE" */
+		cmos_post_code(POSTCODE_RESET_REQUESTED);
+	}
+	if (!(pci_read_config32(PCH_LPC_DEV, PMIR) & PMIR_CF9LOCK))
+		pci_or_config32(PCH_LPC_DEV, PMIR, PMIR_CF9GR);
+	else
+		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "GbE: CF9GR locked, a host reset may not re-enable it\n");
+	full_reset();
+}
+
 void pch_apply_gbe_option(void)
 {
 	const struct device *const gbe = pcidev_on_root(0x19, 0);
@@ -124,9 +146,9 @@ void pch_apply_gbe_option(void)
 	 * The LAN disable bit of BUC lives in the SUS well, which the Function
 	 * Disable lockdown (FDSW bit 7) freezes: a reset after the option is
 	 * toggled still runs with the lockdown set, so the write does not stick.
-	 * Clear the lockdown with a full reset (CF9 0x0E power cycle, which the
-	 * next boot's romstage then precedes before the lockdown is set again),
-	 * as the Lenovo firmware of the W541 does; the write takes on that boot.
+	 * Clear the lockdown with the reset below (which also clears it), so the
+	 * next boot's romstage writes BUC before the lockdown is set again, as
+	 * the Lenovo firmware of the W541 does; the write takes on that boot.
 	 */
 	if (RCBA32(BUC) != want) {
 		if (RCBA32(FDSW) & FDSW_LOCK) {
@@ -137,14 +159,10 @@ void pch_apply_gbe_option(void)
 			return;
 		}
 	} else {
-		printk(BIOS_INFO, "GbE: turned %s, full reset for it to take effect\n",
+		printk(BIOS_INFO, "GbE: turned %s, global reset for it to take effect\n",
 		       on ? "on" : "off");
 	}
-	if (CONFIG(CMOS_POST)) {
-		cmos_post_extra(0x47624500);	/* "GbE" */
-		cmos_post_code(POSTCODE_RESET_REQUESTED);
-	}
-	full_reset();
+	gbe_reset();
 }
 #endif
 
